# inv-patch: 22-l2-thin
# purpose: L2 oracle, the matched thin path pair of spec §5.2 (built on 20's inv_flags architecture): with SPDK_INV_THIN=1 perf selects a thin fn table once (stock nvme_submit_io untouched) whose submit calls spdk_nvme_inv_thin_read() for every read (no nvme_request, no tracker, no generic layer); both arms take the cid from one compact LIFO stack (num_trackers deep) and batch the SQ doorbell like stock, and their completions run in the noinline lever loops; B-thin (mode 0, INV_F_THIN) keeps cb_fn/cb_arg in a per-cid context array, writes the 64 B SQE straight into the SQ slot with four 16 B streaming stores from registers (PRP1 = the task buffer address translated once at init) and consumes CQEs by phase bit; I-thin (mode 4, INV_F_THIN|INV_F_ITHIN) writes the stock-packed 40 B Mode D descriptor and the completion record calls the echoed callback; with the env unset the inv-levers hot paths keep the inv-stock code plus 20's one inv_flags test per poll and per submit
# safety: UNSAFE
# breaks: the generic layer (no nvme_request: no split, retry, abort, timeout, admin); thin IO is invisible to abort, timeout, teardown and iterate_requests, and nvme_pcie_qpair_reset does not re-seed the stack (in-flight IO across a reset is lost); reads only, one ns (the Mode D descriptor carries no nsid); QD per qpair must be <= num_trackers (num_entries - max_completions_cap, 896 with the 1024-entry target queues), beyond that the thin call returns -EAGAIN (perf requeues it under -Q, drops it otherwise); with the env set every IO qpair is thin and must not see generic-path IO (cid collision), so perf fails the run loudly (status 1, draining) instead of falling back: writes, IO over 4 KiB, metadata, IO flags, more than one iovec, or a qpair without thin state (mode C only or Mode E: the library logs and leaves it stock); thin supersedes SPDK_INV_TRFREE on the same qpair; perf page-aligns its buffers while the env is set; the SQ-in-CMB max-access-width quirk is not honored; qpair.queue_depth, num_outstanding_reqs and submitted_requests do not count thin IO; per-IO cycle records are not taken. D1 asymmetry: B-thin carries nsid and PRP1, I-thin carries no data address (D1), so read the pair together with L9 (data-address cost). §4 L evidence: one stderr line per IO qpair at destroy, "INV_THIN qid=N all K cids returned at destroy", or an ERROR line counting lost and extra cids
# env: SPDK_INV_THIN=1 (default off; mode 0 = B-thin, mode 4 = I-thin)
# base: 00-spin.diff,01-floor.diff,10-walk.diff,11-deadstores.diff,12-residue.diff,13-iport.diff,20-l1-trfree.diff
